Z||000004||GodSend||08-24-2001||06:52 PM||||I agree, cheep thrills is a nice place.  Heres how to get there..<P>Shoot down the 401 west towards london ways (its not far though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ... Exit on Highway 25 in milton, and head south on 25 past the macdonalds, past the opp station... Its on your right hand side (about 1 km off the highway) ... Check their hours.. there are a few days they are not open, but I know they are open friday and sat ..<P>Most things are used, but great prices.  Got 2 Dunlop 235-50-16's for 60 bucks for both (60% tread left)... check them out.||||reg||1
Z||000005||grinthock||08-24-2001||07:10 PM||||I keep hearing AMAZING things about them, and I drive by there EVERY DAY on the way home but didn't know they were there... I will stop there next week||||reg||1
Z||000006||banditbalz||08-24-2001||09:56 PM||||There called "Cheap Thrills" and I have bought rims there before. Great selection. The one guy that works there has a silver Fastback GT that looks like my ride. Definately worth the drive.<P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||14
